# Daily Notes

I have never liked keeping records.

Most things worth remembering are better left in memory. The rest are usually things I'd rather forget.

Still, there has been an increasing number of inconsistencies lately.

People remember faces more readily than they remember voices.

They remember names even more readily.

A name is convenient. A face is useful. Neither is proof of identity.

I've been thinking about that more than I should.

Perhaps it is because of the incident.

Perhaps it is because of the body.

I should stop writing about this here.
